  "id": "COMPOUND:2248 - PROTEIN:1725",
  "verbalization": "Myricetin appears to interact with Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein through a multi-step pathway involving secondary targets. The evidence suggests that Myricetin directly targets the Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase, which in turn is a target of Excisusin B. This chain of interactions leads to the final target of Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein. Similarly, Myricetin also targets Peripheral myelin protein 22, which is a target of another compound, 2-(2-((2E)-3,7-Dimethyl-2,6-octadien-1-yl)-5-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)-6-benzofuranol, which also targets Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein. These findings suggest that Myricetin may influence the function of Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein through different molecular mechanisms, potentially involving helicase activity or enzyme regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex network of interactions that Myricetin may engage in, emphasizing its potential role in modulating protein stability and function.",
